ht_1_summary>,\n                \"explanation\": <insight_1_explanation>\n            }},\n            {{\n                \"summary\":<insight_2_summary>,\n                \"explanation\": <insight_2_explanation>\n            }}\n        ]\n    }}\n\n# Grounding Rules\n\nPoints supported by data should list their data references as follows:\n\n\"This is an example sentence supported by multiple data references [Data: <dataset name> (record ids); <dataset name> (record ids)].\"\n\nDo not list more than 5 record ids in a single reference. Instead, list the top 5 most relevant record ids and add \"+more\" to indicate that there are more.\n\nFor example:\n\"Person X is the owner of Company Y and subject to many allegations of wrongdoing [Data: Reports (1), Entities (5, 7); Relationships (23); Claims (7, 2, 34, 64, 46, +more)].\"\n\nwhere 1, 5, 7, 23, 2, 34, 46, and 64 represent the id (not the index) of the relevant data record.\n\nDo not include information where the supporting evidence for it is not provided.\n\n\n# Example Input\n-----------\nText:\n\nEntities\n\nid,entity,description\n5,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,Verdant Oasis Plaza is the location of the Unity March\n6,HARMONY ASSEMBLY,Harmony Assembly is an organization that is holding a march at Verdant Oasis Plaza\n\nRelationships\n\nid,source,target,description\n37,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,UNITY MARCH,Verdant Oasis Plaza is the location of the Unity March\n38,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,HARMONY ASSEMBLY,Harmony Assembly is holding a march at Verdant Oasis Plaza\n39,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,UNITY MARCH,The Unity March is taking place at Verdant Oasis Plaza\n40,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,TRIBUNE SPOTLIGHT,Tribune Spotlight is reporting on the Unity march taking place at Verdant Oasis Plaza\n41,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,BAILEY ASADI,Bailey Asadi is speaking at Verdant Oasis Plaza about the march\n43,HARMONY ASSEMBLY,UNITY MARCH,Harmony Assembly is organizing the Unity March\n\nOutput:\n{{\n    \"title\": \"Verdant Oasis Plaza and Unity March\",\n    \"summary\": \"The community revolves around the Verdant Oasis Plaza, which is the location of the Unity March. The plaza has relationships with the Harmony Assembly, Unity March, and Tribune Spotlight, all of which are associated with the march event.\",\n    \"rating\": 5.0,\n    \"rating_explanation\": \"The impact severity rating is moderate due to the potential for unrest or conflict during the Unity March.\",\n    \"findings\": [\n        {{\n            \"summary\": \"Verdant Oasis Plaza as the central location\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Verdant Oasis Plaza is the central entity in this community, serving as the location for the Unity March. This plaza is the common link between all other entities, suggesting its significance in the community. The plaza's association with the march could potentially lead to issues such as public disorder or conflict, depending on the nature of the march and the reactions it provokes. [Data: Entities (5), Relationships (37, 38, 39, 40, 41,+more)]\"\n        }},\n        {{\n            \"summary\": \"Harmony Assembly's role in the community\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Harmony Assembly is another key entity in this community, being the organizer of the march at Verdant Oasis Plaza. The nature of Harmony Assembly and its march could be a potential source of threat, depending on their objectives and the reactions they provoke. The relationship between Harmony Assembly and the plaza is crucial in understanding the dynamics of this community. [Data: Entities(6), Relationships (38, 43)]\"\n        }},\n        {{\n            \"summary\": \"Unity March as a significant event\",\n            \"explanation\": \"The Unity March is a significant event taking place at Verdant Oasis Plaza. This event is a key factor in the community's dynamics and could be a potential source of threat, depending on the nature of the march and the reactions it provokes. The relationship between the march and the plaza is crucial in understanding the dynamics of this community. [Data: Relationships (39)]\"\n        }},\n        {{\n            \"summary\": \"Role of Tribune Spotlight\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Tribune Spotlight is reporting on the Unity March taking place in Verdant Oasis Plaza. This suggests that the event has attracted media attention, which could amplify its impact on the community. The role of Tribune Spotlight could be significant in shaping public perception of the event and the entities involved. [Data: Relationships (40)]\"\n        }}\n    ]\n}}\n\n\n# Real Data\n\nUse the following text for your answer. Do not make anything up in your answer.\n\nText:\n----Reports-----\ncommunity,full_content\r\n1099,\"# Desnutrición and Oncological Patients\n\nThe community focuses on the critical issue of desnutrición (malnutrition) affecting various patient populations, particularly oncological patients. The entities are interconnected through their relationships, highlighting the importance of nutritional support and interventions in managing health outcomes for these vulnerable groups.\n\n## Desnutrición as a prevalent condition in cancer patients\n\nDesnutrición is a common and serious issue among cancer patients, with prevalence rates reaching up to 50%. This condition arises due to the disease itself and the treatments that patients undergo, necessitating tailored nutritional interventions to support their recovery and overall health. The relationship between desnutrición and cancer is critical, as malnutrition can complicate treatment efficacy and worsen patient outcomes. [Data: Entities (28, 3047, 2516); Relationships (932, 957, 10921)]\n\n## The role of nutritional support in managing desnutrición\n\nNutritional support, including enteral and parenteral nutrition, is essential for patients suffering from desnutrición, especially those unable to meet their caloric needs through oral intake. This support is particularly vital for oncological patients, who often experience increased metabolic demands and challenges in nutrient absorption. The healthcare system aims to identify and address malnutrition through comprehensive nutritional assessments and interventions. [Data: Entities (28, 2336, 3047); Relationships (930, 942, 4809)]\n\n## Impact of dysphagia on nutritional status\n\nDysphagia, or difficulty swallowing, is a significant contributor to desnutrición, particularly in patients with neurological diseases and cancer. This condition can severely limit food intake, leading to inadequate nutrition and subsequent health complications. The interrelationship between dysphagia and malnutrition underscores the need for careful monitoring and dietary interventions to ensure adequate nutrient intake for affected patients. [Data: Entities (28, 13312); Relationships (376, 107)]\n\n## Inmunodepresión linked to malnutrition\n\nInmunodepresión, or immunodeficiency, is often a consequence of desnutrición, particularly in cancer patients. This weakened immune response increases susceptibility to infections and other health complications, further complicating the management of these patients. The relationship between malnutrition and inmunodepresión highlights the critical need for effective nutritional strategies to enhance immune function and overall health outcomes. [Data: Entities (13242); Relationships (973, 19426)]\n\n## Economic implications of desnutrición\n\nDesnutrición significantly impacts healthcare costs, as patients with malnutrition often experience longer hospital stays and increased complications. The costs associated with medical processes can rise due to the need for additional interventions and support for malnourished patients. Addressing malnutrition is not only crucial for improving patient outcomes but also for reducing the economic burden on healthcare systems. [Data: Entities (3230); Relationships (944)]\"\r\n1097,\"# Graft-Versus-Host Disease and Hematopoietic Cell Transplantation\n\nThis community focuses on the medical conditions and treatments associated with graft-versus-host disease (GVHD) following hematopoietic cell transplantation. Key entities include various forms of GVHD, the transplantation procedure itself, and the nutritional support required for patients undergoing these treatments. The relationships among these entities highlight the complexities and risks involved in managing post-transplant complications.\n\n## Graft-versus-host disease as a critical post-transplant complication\n\nGraft-versus-host disease (GVHD) is a significant complication that can arise after hematopoietic cell transplantation, where the transplanted cells attack the recipient's body. This condition can lead to severe morbidity and mortality, making it a critical focus for medical professionals. The acute form of GVHD typically presents within the first few weeks post-transplant, affecting the skin, liver, and intestines, while chronic GVHD can develop later, requiring ongoing management and care. The relationship between GVHD and the transplantation process underscores the importance of monitoring patients closely for signs of this condition. [Data: Entities (13736, 13781, 2333, 19644); Relationships (19644, 19641, 7048)]\n\n## Nutritional support as essential for recovery\n\nNutritional support is crucial for patients undergoing hematopoietic cell transplantation, as they often experience malnutrition due to the treatment and its side effects. Both parenteral and enteral nutrition may be necessary to ensure adequate caloric intake and support recovery. Patients with acute or chronic GVHD may require specialized nutritional interventions to manage their condition effectively. The relationships between nutritional support and the transplantation process highlight the need for a multidisciplinary approach to patient care, integrating nutritional management with medical treatment. [Data: Entities (1647, 2149); Relationships (4820, 6762, 2795, 4818, 4817)]\n\n## Corticosteroids as a primary treatment for GVHD\n\nCorticosteroids are a cornerstone in the treatment of graft-versus-host disease, particularly in managing acute cases. These medications help suppress the immune response that leads to tissue damage in GVHD. However, their use can be associated with significant side effects, including impacts on metabolism and increased risk of infections. The relationship between corticosteroids and GVHD treatment emphasizes the need for careful monitoring and management of potential complications arising from steroid use. [Data: Entities (2149); Relationships (9000, 7052, 9001, 8994)]\n\n## Chronic GVHD requires ongoing management\n\nChronic graft-versus-host disease presents unique challenges as it can manifest long after the initial transplant, often requiring continuous medical intervention. Patients may experience recurrent infections and multi-organ involvement, necessitating a comprehensive management strategy. The relationship between chronic GVHD and the transplantation process highlights the importance of long-term follow-up and care for transplant recipients to improve their quality of life and health outcomes. [Data: Entities (2333, 13736); Relationships (9003, 7050)]\n\n## Hepatic veno-occlusive disease as a post-transplant complication\n\nHepatic veno-occlusive disease is another serious complication that can occur following hematopoietic cell transplantation, affecting liver function and leading to significant morbidity. The incidence of this condition underscores the need for vigilant monitoring of liver health in transplant patients. The relationship between hepatic veno-occlusive disease and the transplantation process highlights the complexities involved in managing post-transplant complications and the importance of a multidisciplinary approach to patient care. [Data: Entities (13782); Relationships (611, 7051)]\"\r\n1100,\"# Hematopoietic Cell Transplantation Community\n\nThe community focuses on hematopoietic cell transplantation, involving various medical procedures, treatments, and research studies. Key entities include procedures like 'Trasplante de Células Hematológicas' and 'Tratamiento Antineoplásico', along with researchers contributing to the field, such as BROWN and AQUINO. The relationships among these entities highlight the importance of nutritional support and the management of complications associated with transplantation.\n\n## Importance of Hematopoietic Cell Transplantation\n\nHematopoietic cell transplantation is a vital medical procedure used to treat various hematological diseases, including certain cancers. This procedure is considered potentially curative and involves the transfer of hematopoietic stem cells, which can restore blood function. The complexity of this treatment necessitates comprehensive care, including high doses of chemotherapy and nutritional support, making it a significant focus within the medical community. [Data: Entities (13735), Relationships (19646, 4418)]\n\n## Role of Nutritional Support\n\nNutritional support is crucial for patients undergoing hematopoietic cell transplantation, as it can significantly impact recovery and overall health. Both parenteral and enteral nutrition methods are employed to meet the nutritional needs of patients who may not be able to eat normally due to treatment side effects. The relationships between nutritional assessment and the transplantation process underscore the importance of maintaining nutritional status during treatment. [Data: Entities (13735), Relationships (4816, 2793, 4303)]\n\n## Complications Associated with Transplantation\n\nHematopoietic cell transplantation is associated with several serious complications, including graft-versus-host disease (GVHD) and veno-occlusive disease. These complications can significantly affect patient outcomes and require careful monitoring and management. Understanding these risks is essential for healthcare providers to improve patient care and treatment strategies. [Data: Entities (13779, 13737), Relationships (19644, 19645)]\n\n## Research Contributions to Glutamine Administration\n\nSeveral researchers, including BROWN and AQUINO, have investigated the effects of glutamine administration in patients undergoing hematopoietic transplantation. Their studies aim to understand how glutamine can influence recovery and mortality rates, highlighting the ongoing research efforts to optimize treatment protocols and improve patient outcomes. [Data: Entities (3016, 13811), Relationships (10868, 19650, 19651)]\n\n## Impact of Chemotherapy in Transplantation\n\nChemotherapy plays a critical role in the hematopoietic cell transplantation process, as it is administered in high doses to prepare the patient for the infusion of stem cells. This treatment is essential for eradicating malignant cells but also poses risks of severe side effects, including nutritional deficiencies and increased susceptibility to infections. Understanding the balance between effective treatment and managing side effects is crucial for patient care. [Data: Entities (632, 13735), Relationships (896, 4418)]\"\r\n1101,\"# Infections and Morbidity in Critical Care\n\nThis community focuses on the interrelated issues of infections, morbidity, and mortality in critically ill patients, particularly those undergoing transplantation and suffering from chronic conditions. Key entities include infections, chronic liver disease, and the impact of malnutrition, highlighting the complex interplay between these factors in patient health outcomes.\n\n## Infections as a critical health challenge\n\nInfections are a major concern in critically ill patients, particularly those undergoing hematopoietic cell transplants due to immunosuppression. The risk of infections can lead to increased morbidity and mortality, necessitating careful management strategies. Infections are prevalent in various patient populations, including those with chronic liver diseases and malnutrition, which further complicates their health status. [Data: Entities (2330, 10159, 54, 2328, 9581); Relationships (9581, 2735, 577, 7264, 1354)]\n\n## The role of malnutrition in morbidity and mortality\n\nMalnutrition significantly contributes to increased morbidity and mortality rates, especially among the elderly and critically ill patients. Conditions such as EHC (chronic liver disease) and dysphagia are closely linked to malnutrition, which can exacerbate health complications. Effective nutritional support is essential to mitigate these risks and improve patient outcomes. [Data: Entities (10159, 54, 12872); Relationships (759, 7264, 956, 1358, 1356)]\n\n## Impact of chronic liver disease on patient health\n\nPatients with chronic liver disease, particularly those experiencing sarcopenia, face heightened risks of infections and complications that can lead to increased morbidity and mortality. The nutritional status of these patients is critical, as it influences their overall health and recovery outcomes. [Data: Entities (10159, 54); Relationships (18206, 7164, 1339)]\n\n## Morbidity and mortality linked to surgical interventions\n\nMorbimortalidad is a significant concern in the context of surgical procedures, where complications such as infections can arise. The relationship between surgical interventions and patient outcomes emphasizes the need for careful monitoring and nutritional support to reduce risks associated with these procedures. [Data: Entities (54, 12872); Relationships (258, 131, 1359)]\n\n## The significance of nutritional strategies in infection prevention\n\nNutritional strategies, particularly enteral nutrition, have been shown to reduce the risk of infections in various clinical contexts. Early enteral nutrition can significantly lower the incidence of post-surgical infections, highlighting the importance of integrating nutritional management into patient care protocols. [Data: Entities (2330); Relationships (2735)]\"\r\n\n\n-----Entities-----\nhuman_readable_id,title,description,degree\r\n597,VALORACIÓN NUTRICIONAL,\"\"\"VALORACIÓN NUTRICIONAL\"\" refers to a comprehensive process aimed at evaluating the nutritional status of individuals, particularly those at risk of malnutrition due to various medical conditions. This assessment is crucial for detecting early signs of malnutrition, especially in patients with oropharyngeal dysphagia, inflammatory bowel disease, liver diseases, and those undergoing treatments such as cancer therapies or hematopoietic cell transplants.\n\nThe process involves a variety of measurements and markers, including clinical and anthropometric evaluations, to understand a patient's dietary habits and nutritional needs. It is a dynamic and ongoing procedure that not only identifies the risk of malnutrition but also establishes the necessity for nutritional interventions. The nutritional assessment is essential for guiding dietary and health interventions, ensuring that patients receive appropriate support tailored to their specific conditions.\n\nIn particular, the nutritional assessment is integral to protocols for managing dysphagia and is conducted by specialized teams, such as the UNCyD team, to ensure comprehensive care. This systematic approach to evaluating dietary intake and nutritional status is vital for the effective management of patients, especially those in critical conditions or with complex health needs.\",30\r\n2302,SOPORTE NUTRICIONAL,\"SOPORTE NUTRICIONAL, or nutritional support, is a vital intervention aimed at enhancing the tolerance to treatment and improving the quality of life for patients suffering from malnutrition. It is particularly crucial for individuals who have undergone metabolic surgery, especially those experiencing complications. Nutritional support plays a significant role in the management of various health conditions, including cancer and dementia, as it helps to improve overall health outcomes.\n\nThis support is designed to meet the dietary needs of patients who are unable to eat normally, including those with intestinal failure and critically ill patients. It encompasses a range of methods and practices to provide nutrition, especially for patients who cannot consume food orally. Nutritional support is also essential in clinical settings for individuals with eating disorders and is particularly important for children who require assistance in meeting their dietary needs.\n\nOverall, SOPORTE NUTRICIONAL is a comprehensive approach to ensuring that patients receive the necessary dietary assistance to enhance their clinical outcomes and overall well-being.\",16\r\n2107,DIETA POLIMÉRICA,\"DIETA POLIMÉRICA refers to a polymeric diet, which is a form of enteral nutrition designed for patients who can digest food normally. This diet contains whole proteins and offers a balanced mix of nutrients, making it suitable for individuals with specific dietary needs. It is commonly utilized in clinical settings to support the nutritional requirements of patients.\",2\r\n1753,FUNCIONES INMUNITARIAS,Immune functions are biological processes that can be affected by malnutrition and are assessed through various nutritional markers.,3\r\n13742,AUTÓLOGO,\"AUTÓLOGO refers to a type of bone marrow transplantation in which the donor is the patient themselves. This procedure utilizes the patient's own hematological cells, thereby avoiding issues related to compatibility.\",3\r\n201,PACIENTES HOSPITALIZADOS,\"\"\"PACIENTES HOSPITALIZADOS\"\" refers to individuals who are receiving treatment in a hospital setting. This group is particularly vulnerable to various health complications, including a notable percentage diagnosed with dysphagia, which is a condition that affects swallowing. Additionally, hospitalized patients are at a high risk of malnutrition, a prevalent issue that can further complicate their overall health status.\",3\r\n15427,PACIENTES PEDIÁTRICOS,,3\r\n13740,CÉLULAS HEMATOLÓGICAS,\"CÉLULAS HEMATOLÓGICAS son las células de la sangre que desempeñan un papel crucial en los trasplantes, utilizados para tratar diversas enfermedades hematológicas.\",6\r\n1754,ENFERMEDADES HEMATOLÓGICAS,\"Enfermedades hematológicas are blood disorders that affect the blood and the organs responsible for blood production. These conditions can lead to excessive production of ácido úrico due to high cellular turnover and can influence lymphocyte counts and overall nutritional status. Treatment for hematological diseases may involve hematopoietic cell transplantation, which is a procedure used to replace damaged or diseased blood-forming cells.\",4\r\n1723,EDMAS/ASCITIS,,1\r\n7161,MARCADORES ANTROPOMÉTRICOS,Los marcadores antropométricos son medidas físicas que ayudan a evaluar el estado nutricional de un paciente.,1\r\n7160,MARCADORES CLÍNICOS,Los marcadores clínicos son utilizados en la valoración nutricional para identificar el grado de desnutrición en pacientes.,1\r\n6978,VARÓN DE 76 AÑOS,,6\r\n15967,DISPOSITIVO DE ALIMENTACIÓN,Dispositivo de alimentación refers to medical devices used to deliver nutrition directly to the stomach or intestines of patients who cannot eat normally.,3\r\n12926,GUÍAS ESPEN,Guías ESPEN are guidelines provided by the European Society for Clinical Nutrition and Metabolism regarding nutritional support in clinical settings.,1\r\n12501,INSUFICIENCIA INTESTINAL,,1\r\n15973,INTRODUCCIÓN EN VENA PERIFÉRICA,Introducción en vena periférica de sustancia nutricional is a medical procedure for delivering nutritional substances directly into the peripheral veins of patients.,1\r\n12925,RECOMENDACIONES SEMICYUC,Recomendaciones SEMICYUC are guidelines developed by the SEMICYUC for nutritional support in critically ill patients.,1\r\n6976,DIETA HIPERCALÓRICA,\"The \"\"DIETA HIPERCALÓRICA\"\" refers to a hypercaloric diet, which is a high-calorie dietary regimen specifically designed to provide an increased energy intake. This type of diet is often preferred for patients who require volume restriction, making it suitable for individuals with specific health needs. Additionally, it is commonly utilized for patients experiencing malnutrition, as it aims to help them gain weight and improve their overall nutritional status.\",2\r\n13745,CORDÓN UMBILICAL,\"El cordón umbilical es una fuente de células madre hematopoyéticas que se utilizan en trasplantes, especialmente en niños.\",1\r\n13743,MEDULA ÓSEA,La médula ósea es el tejido donde se producen las células sanguíneas y de donde se obtienen células para trasplantes.,1\r\n13744,SANGRE PERIFÉRICA,La sangre periférica es la sangre que circula en el cuerpo y de la cual se pueden obtener células hematológicas mediante aféresis.,1\r\n13746,HÍGADO FETAL,El hígado fetal es un órgano de donde se pueden obtener células hematopoyéticas en casos específicos de trasplante.,1\r\n6975,ICTUS VERTEBRO-BASILAR,\"A vertebrobasilar stroke is a type of stroke that affects the brainstem and can lead to various complications, including dysphagia.\",1\r\n6977,TRATAMIENTO ANTIDEPRESIVO,\"Antidepressant treatment is a medical intervention aimed at managing symptoms of depression, which can affect a patient's appetite and nutritional intake.\",1\r\n10080,IRC,\"Chronic kidney disease (IRC) is a long-term condition where the kidneys do not work effectively, requiring dietary management.\",3\r\n15979,INSERCIÓN EN ESTÓMAGO,Inserción en estómago de dispositivo de alimentación is a procedure for placing a feeding device directly into the stomach for nutritional delivery.,1\r\n15980,INSERCIÓN EN YEYUNO,Inserción en yeyuno de dispositivo de alimentación is a method for placing a feeding device into the jejunum for direct nutritional support.,1\r\n1755,ENFERMEDADES HEPATOPÁTICAS,Hepatopathies are liver diseases that can impact nutritional assessments and immune function.,1\r\n10078,DIETA HIPOPROTEICA,\"A hypoproteic diet is a dietary regimen that restricts protein intake, often recommended for patients with renal insufficiency.\",1\r\n10079,POLIQUISTOSIS RENAL,